From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kangaroo maintainers
Date: 2026-10-15
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: export WebProcessExtensionManager via WK_EXPORT for the
 injected bundle

CLANG64/CLANGARM64 CI (Round 40) fails at the webkitgtkinjectedbundle link:

  ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: WebKit::WebProcessExtensionManager::singleton()
  ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: WebKit::WebProcessExtensionManager::initialize(WebKit::InjectedBundle*, API::Object*)
  >>> referenced by WebKitInjectedBundleMain.cpp.obj:(WKBundleInitialize)

Root cause
----------
webkitglib-symbols.map defines the entire C++ export surface of
libwebkitgtk-6.0: the three *ProcessMain entry points plus
WebProcessExtensionManager::singleton()/initialize(). The three ProcessMain
declarations (Source/WebKit/{WebProcess,NetworkProcess,GPUProcess}/*Main.h)
already use WK_EXPORT, which on Windows expands to __declspec(dllexport)
while building the WebKit library (BUILDING_WebKit) and to
__declspec(dllimport) in consumers. WebProcessExtensionManager.h instead
decorates the two methods with a raw __attribute__((visibility("default"))):
on ELF that is a genuine export mechanism (and the version script keeps the
two symbols global), but on PE/COFF the attribute exports nothing. Because
libwebkitgtk-6.0.dll already contains explicit dllexport symbols
(WEBKIT_API / WK_EXPORT C API), linker auto-export is disabled for it, so
the two methods are missing from the DLL export table and from
libwebkitgtk-6.0.dll.a; lld (strict on undefined symbols in -shared links)
then fails the webkitgtkinjectedbundle module, whose only TU references
exactly those two symbols. The three process executables linked fine
because their cross-DLL C++ surface (the *ProcessMain trio) is already
WK_EXPORT-decorated.

Fix
---
Declare both methods with WK_EXPORT and include WKDeclarationSpecifiers.h,
mirroring the sibling WebKitWebProcessExtensionPrivate.h (which already
exports webkitWebProcessExtensionSetGarbageCollectOnPageDestroy the same
way). On Linux WK_EXPORT expands to the same visibility("default")
attribute, so the ELF export surface is unchanged; on MinGW the two symbols
become dllexport'd from libwebkitgtk-6.0.dll (and gc-rooted under
--gc-sections, since export-table entries are collector roots) and are
consumed via the import library in webkitgtkinjectedbundle.dll.

Verified
--------
- PE/COFF shape matrix (clang 19 --target={x86_64,aarch64}-w64-windows-gnu
  + ld.lld MinGW flavor, -shared --gc-sections, import library generated):
  PRE shape reproduces both undefined-symbol errors verbatim and the
  symbols are absent from the DLL/import library; POST shape links the
  bundle, exports both symbols (mangled names match the CI error),
  and WKBundleInitialize remains exported from the bundle module.
- ELF no-op check: with -fvisibility=hidden + the webkitglib-symbols.map
  version script, PRE and POST produce an identical dynamic symbol table.

---
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/InjectedBundle/API/glib/WebProcessExtensionManager.h
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/InjectedBundle/API/glib/WebProcessExtensionManager.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #pragma once
 
 #include "Module.h"
+#include "WKDeclarationSpecifiers.h"
 #include <wtf/NeverDestroyed.h>
 #include <wtf/Noncopyable.h>
 #include <wtf/Vector.h>
@@ -43,9 +44,17 @@
 class WebProcessExtensionManager {
     WTF_MAKE_NONCOPYABLE(WebProcessExtensionManager);
 public:
-    __attribute__((visibility("default"))) static WebProcessExtensionManager& singleton();
+    // MinGW/PE port note (kangaroo Round 40): the raw visibility("default")
+    // attribute is ELF-only as an export mechanism. The MinGW port replicates
+    // the webkitglib-symbols.map export surface via WK_EXPORT, which expands
+    // to __declspec(dllexport) when building the WebKit library and
+    // __declspec(dllimport) in the webkitgtkinjectedbundle module (and any
+    // other consumer), mirroring how WebProcessMain.h already declares the
+    // other C++ symbols exported by that map. On ELF WK_EXPORT is the same
+    // visibility("default") attribute, so Linux behavior is unchanged.
+    WK_EXPORT static WebProcessExtensionManager& singleton();
 
-    __attribute__((visibility("default"))) void initialize(InjectedBundle*, API::Object*);
+    WK_EXPORT void initialize(InjectedBundle*, API::Object*);
 
     WebKitWebProcessExtension* extension() const { return m_extension.get(); }
 
